  "interpretation": [
    "Negative cross-entropy differences favor the named arm; no significance claim.",
    "The frozen no-adapter model is the shared zero-update baseline. All four arms have zero independent local/history feature gates and start at identity. Seeds vary paired minibatch order and finite-budget coverage.",
    "Seeds share evaluation blocks; blocks are not independent experimental replicas.",
    "The ordinary lag1 control has 1536 total/trainable parameters. Fixed-one GL has 1537 total/1536 trainable, with one real frozen order scalar. Both learned-order arms have 1537 trainable parameters. No dummy parameters; learning order adds capacity.",
    "lag1 uses ordinary Torch h[t]=-x[t-1], h[0]=0. At alpha=step=1 Rust strictly-past GL is the same map. Fixed-one versus lag1 is implementation parity, not independent quality evidence. Require exact per-step losses, common gate-gradient receipts, development scores, final gate/Adam states and per-block endpoints for this frozen CPU-f32 protocol.",
    "Learned-one starts at alpha=1 but retains the full Rust order derivative, including older-lag terms. Learned-half starts at alpha=0.5 and reruns the preceding study's learned-history recipe. Different initial orders change filter initialization and conditioning, not only final order.",
    "Primary contrasts: fixed-one minus lag1 for parity; learned-one minus fixed-one for learned departure from a one-lag filter; learned-half minus learned-one for initialization; learned-half minus lag1 for the earlier recipe against ordinary lag mixing.",
    "Complete all twelve 512-update runs and exact next-update continuation before endpoint evaluation. Development scores do not select hyperparameters, checkpoints or run length. Preserve mismatches and losing outcomes.",
    "Pride/Alice are reused exploratory endpoints, not untouched confirmation. Prior results are historical references, not additional independent replicas. No significance, unique fractional-memory advantage or general-LLM claim from a small quality difference.",
    "CPU float32, frozen local GPT-2, full unpadded contexts, no KV cache. History resets at each 128-token block. All arms retain the shared K=32 input budget; the ordinary map actually uses one past tap. Additional host transport or work is not a throughput benchmark.",
    "This summary checks published receipts, not checkpoint contents or process termination.",
    "No speed or pristine-corpus generalization claim."
  ],
